6. **Tests.** Run `/record-fixture <wrapper> <case> <parameters>` for at least one
   realistic case, or `/record-fixture <task> <case> <parameters>` for a task that sends
   more than one request, which records each of its exchanges under the task's name with
   core's `record_task`, add a replay test in `tests/test_tasks.py` using the
   `replay_fixture` fixture, and a `@pytest.mark.live` smoke test in `tests/test_live.py`. The replay
   tests of a family of tasks may live in a module of the source's own beside
   `tests/test_tasks.py`: `copier update` never touches a file the template has never
   rendered, and `tests/test_tasks.py` itself is the source's once rendered. A replay
   test that checks what was sent compares `xippios.core.testing.sent_query(route)`, the
   scrubbed query of the last request, `sent_urls(route)`, the URLs with credentials
   redacted, or `sent_bodies(route)`, the bodies decoded, a JSON body as it parses and a
   form as a mapping of its fields, credentials redacted, never a request kept from
   `route.calls`, which a failure or `pytest -l` would print.
   A test that builds an answer or changes a recorded one, rather than replaying it as
   recorded, says where the body comes from and names its kind in a docstring or a block of
   comments that reaches it, `NOT RECORDED: <where it comes from> (conventions §10, kind 2)`,
   a replay for another request than its recording names `kind 3`, and a value handed to
   the code that no route serves says so in the sentence
   `<the value> is an input of the test, not an answer from <upstream>.` in place of a
   kind. `tests/test_built_answers.py` collects core's check of that mark, which fails
   an unmarked place by its file and line, and names in `READERS` the source's own functions
   that take a body written in a test (conventions §10, sdk-core ADR-0049).
